{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1468399","title":"Intermittent versus continuous ultra-low aeration in low-strength wastewater: Selective regulation of microbial structure and functional potential","description":"Transitioning wastewater treatment toward carbon neutrality necessitates low-oxygen aeration, yet the ecological consequences of different oxygen-restricting strategies on nitrifying communities remain poorly understood. Given that continuous and intermittent aeration impose distinct ecological selection pressures, their differential impacts on the adaptation and succession of ammonia-oxidizing bacteria (AOB) and nitrite-oxidizing bacteria (NOB) are unclear. This study systematically compared intermittent aeration and continuous ultra-low aeration in sequencing batch reactors. Intermittent aeration successfully achieved partial nitrification, strategically engineering oxygen pulse patterns likely provides a more effective selective strategy for advancing carbon-neutral wastewater treatment.","center":"GUangzhou university","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2026/05/19 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN60279508","Metagenome or environmental sample from sludge metagenome","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2023-11-14",2023,"CN","Guangdong",1809858,"Guangzhou","verified",null,null,"China: Guangzhou","sludge",null,null,null,"city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN60279509","Metagenome or environmental sample from sludge metagenome","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2023-11-30",2023,"CN","Guangdong",1809858,"Guangzhou","verified",null,null,"China: Guangzhou","sludge",null,null,null,"city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN60279510","Metagenome o